It tells the story of an alcoholic wagon master who leads a group of
misfit settlers in the Wild West back to the East.

15
01:06:52,500 --> 01:06:58,500
The film was released in the United States on August 26, 1994.

16
01:11:20,000 --> 01:11:26,000
Filming took place in Sierra de Órganos National Park in the town
of Sombrerete, Mexico, and in Durango, Mexico.

17
01:15:47,500 --> 01:15:53,500
During the final days of the film's production in Durango, Mexico,
John Candy died of a heart attack at the age of 43.

18
01:20:15,000 --> 01:20:21,000
Script re-writes, a stand-in and special effects were used to complete his
remaining scenes, and it was released five months after his death.

19
01:24:42,500 --> 01:24:48,500
The film marked Candy's penultimate performance, with the film being dedicated in memory of him as well as
the film being the last Carolco Pictures production to be distributed by TriStar Pictures.

20
01:29:10,000 --> 01:29:16,000
The film was panned by critics, with a rare 0% rating on Rotten Tomatoes.

21
01:33:37,500 --> 01:33:43,500
The film grossed $4.4 million at the box office.

